*---------------------------------------------------------------
* sc.fdact.equ -- fdactions opcodes (ABI FRICTION item 10):
* the 3-byte spawn()-time fd-inheritance records sh's pipeline
* redirection builds and the kernel's PRC_FDACTIONS (in
* procfile2.s) replays. Split out of inc/syscall.equ (task
* #8, docs/SELFHOST-CONVERSION.md phase 1) -- reference-set scan
* shows only sh.s among src/bin/*.s programs needs this; every
* other utility program neither builds nor replays an fdactions
* list. See docs/SYSCALL.md "Item 10" for the full design.
*
* `put`-only file (no code/org/dsk), same precondition
* discipline as memmap.equ -- the top-level file must `put`
* this directly.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

* -- fdactions opcodes (ABI FRICTION item 10, DEFINED here).
* Each record -- is 3 bytes: [opcode][target fd][source fd or
* 0]. See docs/SYSCALL.md -- "Item 10" for the full design and
* the sh pipeline worked example. -- Unaffected by the ProDOS
* ruling (fd numbers are still 0/1/2 + kernel- -- assigned small
* integers at this layer, translated to MLI refnums --
* internally -- fdactions never sees a refnum).
FDACT_END   equ   0     ;list terminator (also: a NULL fdactions
                        ;pointer means "no actions" without
                        ;needing even one byte)
FDACT_DUP   equ   1     ;child[target fd] = dup(parent[source
                        ;fd]), source always resolved against
                        ;the PARENT's table as of spawn() time
                        ;(never a fd a prior action in the SAME
                        ;list just created)
FDACT_CLOSE equ   2     ;child[target fd] = closed (source fd
                        ;byte unused, reserved 0)
